      },
      "worked": "Since $x^2$ and $y^2$ are non-negative, both $x^2<5$ and $y^2<5$. Thus $x,y\\in\\{-2,-1,0,1,2\\}$.\n\nFor $x=\\pm2$, $y^2<1$, so $y=0$: 2 pairs.\n\nFor $x=\\pm1$, $y^2<4$, so $y=-1,0,1$: 6 pairs.\n\nFor $x=0$, $y^2<5$, so $y=-2,-1,0,1,2$: 5 pairs.\n\n$$2+6+5=13.$$\n\nThere are 13 solutions.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
